  "articleBody": "Embarking on a bathroom tile project? Awesome! But let's chat about a few common blunders people make so you can totally avoid them. One major one is trying to install tile over an uneven or damaged base. Trust me, the foundation is everything – if it's not right, your tile won't be either, and you could end up with cracks. Another big no-no, especially in showers or splash zones, is poor waterproofing. You absolutely need to make sure those areas are properly sealed to prevent hidden water damage. Choosing the wrong mortar or grout can also lead to problems down the road, as different tiles and areas require specific types. Don't rush the spacing or alignment either; uneven lines stick out like a sore thumb! And here's a big one: skipping movement joints or sealing where it’s needed. These details protect your tile work from shifting and moisture. When you're dealing with wet areas, large-format tiles, or any substrate repairs, getting a qualified professional involved is usually the smartest move. HH Remodeling in the greater Denver area can help ensure your tile project is done right, from start to finish.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
